   "source": [
    "From the plot we see that the SGD method when gamma = 0.1 is ahead early for a few single point gradient evaluations, but that the full batch gradient descent quickly catches up. The SGD method when gamma = 0.02 is on the contrary ahead late, which points to the step-size affecting this. We see that neither of the SGD methods converge, and that they plateu, with the most error being for larger stepsize gamma = 0.1. The full batch gradient descent is the only method that converges. This comes from the fact that SGD has a gradient noise that never decays, and when using a constant learning rate gamma the iterations eventually just bounce around the minimum.\n",
    "When a larger stepsize is used, the noise causes the gradient descent to travel further from the correct direction when the noise affects the gradient value. It might cost less per step, causing SGD to be more effective at the start, but eventually full batch GD catches up and actually converges."
